    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιχάσκω</span></b> , impf., v.
		infr.: aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφέχᾰνον</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gape round, gape for,</i> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμὲ μὲν Κὴρ ἀμφέχανε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.79
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστὸν ἀμφέχασκ᾽ ἐμόν,</span>
			of an infant, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				545
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιχανὼν λόγχαις ἑπτάπυλον
				στόμα,</span> of the Argive army round Thebes, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				118
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκίστρου . . πλάνον
				ἀμφιχανοῦσα,</span> of a fish, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.702
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>): rarely c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				3.178
			</span></i>.</div>
